 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "The BBC showed Swiss farmers picking spaghetti off trees.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.022
  },
  {
   "text": "Noodles dangled from every branch, and families yanked them down.",
   "s": 3.322,
   "e": 6.511
  },
  {
   "text": "Then they laid the spaghetti out in the sun to dry.",
   "s": 6.811,
   "e": 8.866
  },
  {
   "text": "The reporter said a mild winter meant a bumper crop.",
   "s": 9.166,
   "e": 11.649
  },
  {
   "text": "Even the dreaded spaghetti weevil was gone.",
   "s": 11.95,
   "e": 13.808
  },
  {
   "text": "Eight million people watched. Hundreds still believed it.",
   "s": 14.108,
   "e": 16.719
  },
  {
   "text": "So the phones exploded: how do I grow my own spaghetti tree?",
   "s": 17.019,
   "e": 19.807
  },
  {
   "text": "The BBC's answer?",
   "s": 20.577,
   "e": 21.616
  },
  {
   "text": "Put a sprig of spaghetti in tomato sauce, and hope for the best.",
   "s": 22.036,
   "e": 25.096
  },
  {
   "text": "The date the BBC showed those trees? April the first.",
   "s": 25.396,
   "e": 28.393
  }
 ],
